<title>AUSTRIA: Austria finmin says no plans to revalue reserves.</title>
<headline>Austria finmin says no plans to revalue reserves.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Austrian finance ministry said it had no plans to change the valuation of the country's gold reserves, held by the Austrian National Bank.</p>
<p>&quot;There are no such plans,&quot; a ministry spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>According to official statistics, the Austrian central bank held some 316 tons of gold reserves valued at 18.98 billion schillings at the end of April. -- Vienna newsroom, +431 53112 274</p>
